\subsubsection{Subsubsection}

There are four section-level-types in this UAH format that will
appear in the TOC:
\begin{enumerate}
\item Chapter
\item Section
\item Subsection
\item Subsubsection
\end{enumerate}

\noindent where, as far as numbering is concerned, in the book class
of files, \LaTeX\ considers ``chapter'' to be zero, ``section'' to
be 1, and so on. More section-levels exist (\ie, ``Paragraph''
follows subsubsection), and you can use them in the text of your
thesis, but you will have to edit the \verb|uahdis.sty| file to
enable them in the TOC (and, I would not suggest putting anything
below a subsubsection in the TOC).

